Much of this game has been discussed in the recent "At the Gates of
Gehennom!" thread in this group.  However I'm so happy that I'm going
to subject all of you to the full story (besides it's easy enough to
move on to the next thread in your newsreader).

I have been playing nethack for about a year. On my computer main
computer I have in the logfile 710 games.  On alt.org (under various
char
names), I have about 150 more games and on my other computer I have
around 250-300 games. Total number of games played is around 1100.

It was May 2006 when I got my first character beyond both Soko and the
Mines.  He made it all the way down to the castle and beyond, but died
before reaching the Gates of Gehennom. It was shortly after that I had
my first char actually get the amulet, but fail to ascend.  However
since then, I haven't had a character get past both the mines and
Soko.

Finally last week I had one break that curse of dead chars.

Here's the blow by blow account.  I'm sure the experienced players
will have a lot to laugh at and suggest better ways of doing this.

Our hero, Globnar the Orc Wizard, found the mines entrance early on
but skipped them to look for Soko.  He quickly learned how useful the
sleep spell is (even better than force bolt). A rock trap took out
kitten early on, but three dogs (known as the Puppy Dogs of Doom)
joined soon after.  However the good luck didn't last.  Our hero
continued down without finding any alters or much food.

Somewhere around dlvl5, our hero encountered a newt and killed
it. Being hungry and without food, he quickly ate the corpse.  Wait a
minute, the screen didn't say newt, it said camealon!  I watched in
horror as Our hero underwent a frightning horrible change.  His
studded leather armor and cloak of magic resistance were ripped to
shreads as he became some terrible beast.  "Oh great Anhur save me
from this," cried out our hero.  Fortunatly Anhur was pleased and
returned our hero to orcish form. Our hero proceeded now without his
two best pieces of armor.

Then on dlvl8 tough resistance was encountered. Hordes of all sorts of
'a's attacked.  Killer bees, giant ants, solider ants, and even some
giant beetles.  Fortunatly our hero remember to engrave the E-word.
It didn't work very well since all he had was his finger to write in
the dust.  However thanks to the sleep spell it wasn't as bad as it
could have been.

Finally our hero takes out the last solider ant and proceeds down the
coridor.  Lo and Behold it is Delphi.  Yikkes!  It looks like someone
took a bee hive and polymorphed them all into various elves.  What to
do??  They don't seem to respect the E-word.  They seem immune to the
sleep spell!  Run!  Fortunatly the three puppies sprung into action,
while our hero ran to the upstairs and closed the door to the room.

Several noises and one "You feel sad for a moment" later our hero has
recovered enough Pw to venture out again.  The carnage must have been
terrible.  The two large dogs sit atop a mountain of equipment. No
bodies in sight.  Unfortunatly none of the equipment is really of much
use.  There were some stealth boots our hero snagged and then off to
explore the rest of Delphi.

WTF?!? another hord of solider ants?!? Rrrruuuuunnnnnn!!!!  Too late.
Our hero is suck in the middle of the central chamber and starts
scribbling the E-word in the dust.  The ants scatter.  Our hero takes
a step and sees a hord of fire ants coming to reinforce the solider
ants.

After trying to scribble the E-word a couple of times, our hero
realizes it has been ages since he ate. In fact he was feeling like he
was going to pass out from hunger.  What happened to that food ration
he found earlier?  Oh that's right he ate it already.  $#@@#$%

It was really starting to look bleak.  What can be done?  Fortunatly
great Anhur interviened.  Then one of the PDoD's killed a fire ant.
Our hero rushed over and feasted on the corpse.  Ooops our hero forgot
moving from his E-word square could be fatal.  Scribble scribble
scribble in the dust.

Pw slowly recovered as the PDoD's took out another ant.  Our hero
finally had enough for a couple of force bolts.  He waited carfully
until the ants lined up and zapped them good. Well good enough for the
PDoD's to finish them off.

Finally this wave of ants was cleared out.  Decideing not to explore
until his Pw had recovered, our hero ran over to the upstairs and
closed the door to the room. If only he could find a key to lock it,
he would be so much safer.

$#@@#$@# why did he have to think about that?  Suddenly the door opens
and a horde of Z's enter.  Lucikly a couple of taps with his mightly
quarterstaff of doom and this horde was defeated.

With Pw only half way recovered, our hero decides it is imparative to
get off this level and find the food in Soko.  This meant skipping the
shattering of the statues.

Away he goes.  Resistance lightend up a little.  There was an orc
horde, but all excpet one of them recognized our hero as a
friend. It's great how orc's can be canniables and no one will care.
Ah finally the down stairs.  Our hero waits for the PDoD's.

Gosh there's an awful lot of noise comeing from the other room. Maybe
our hero should check it out?  He does and is shocked by the horror.
The PDoD's have taken out all except one of the orc horde.  The last
one is cornered by the two.  Oh it won't last long now.  RIP to the
orcs.  On the bright side our hero did scavenge an orcish helm
finally.

The next level Soko was found quickly.  The next level also had a lot
of food and random potions.  Our hero made a temporary stash on the
first level of Soko.

Soko proved to be uneventful. A Cloak of Displacement was picked up,
but that was it.  Soko also proved to be rather devoid of food.  Our
hero found enough to survive, but that was it.  If the lvl below Soko
didn't have all that food, our hero might be in trouble.  The top level
was
the BoH version.  The PDoD's had fun in the zoo and found a friend to
replace the one that had been killed earlier.  In Soko, our hero also
picked up a lamp which would later be discovered to be magic.

With Soko done, our hero went back up to the mines.  He was quite
worried over the fact that his AC was still only 7 and that he had
only a couple of daggers to suppliment his force bolts.

Fortunatly the billions of gnomes and dwarves in the mines proved no
match against the Mighty Quarterstaff of Doom.  Our hero also found a
couple of amulets on the first level of the mines.  Neither were
cursed and neither seemed to do anything bad.

It was only a few levels to the town.  To our hero's dismay, the
temple was to Ptah and not mighty Anhur.  He was still too much of a
weakling to remedy this sistuation.  So he left the filthy Ptah Priest
and his filty alter alone.

The shops didn't have anything of great use, so our hero continued
down.

The next level our hero finally found a dwarf with a pick-axe that
wasn't cursed.  He also picked up a lockpick.  One of the PDoD's
stepted on a poly trap and became a feezing sphere.  Our hero left the
poor thing there.

Shortly after that our hero arrives in the Gnome King's Wine Cellar.
Now this wasn't exactly good.  A bunch of vampire bats attacked. Then
later our hero found what sent the bats, an evil V.  I was quite
supprized when this lowly V sucked two levels from our hero.  However
I was even more supprized when a barrow wright appeared and sucked two
more levels from our hero.  I didn't know a barrow wright could do
this!

In spite of loosing 4 levels, our hero continued onward.  He never
found the Gnome King, but he did take all of the King's booze.  He
found three gray stones.  The booze he dipped in the fountain so he'd
have water ready to become holy.

Back up to the town.  A quick stop to buy the candles then a closer
look at the trees.  Now I've never known what good the trees are. I've
always assumed if I had a real axe, I could chop 'em down and
something cool would be found.  Our hero decides to kick them.  Wow
look at all those bananas!  What does the other one have? Tons of
apples!.

Unfortunatly our hero knows how unfilling these are.  Great for
feeding a horse or monkey but that's about it.  Wonder what happens if
he kicks it again.  @#$@#@#$ NO!  Bees!  Well that wasn't so bad.
What do we get kicking the other tree again?  More bees!  Well that
again wasn't so bad.  Kicking more brought nothing except a low hum or
something.

So back to the main branch to find, the Ft. and the quest.

Our hero continued down.  On and on and on.  The dungeon seemed
bottomless.  The boots of stealh proved useful in killing a leprachuan
hall, a bee hive, and one throne room.  The hive had enough royal
jelly to get our hero up to 18/05 str (there would be a few giants
later which would have his str reach 18/50).  But there wasn't much
else to note.  Equipment continued to be sparce and our hero still had
an AC over 5. The PDoD's met their end at the hands of random nasties
and were not replaced.  There were a few vaults here and there with
lots of $, but nowhere to spend that $.

Things were looking bleak in spite of being further down in the
dungeon that my previous 500 or so attempts. Then finally our hero
gets a faint telepahtic message on dlvl14. He finds the ic portal. He
knows Nefert is in trouble, but what he sees on the other side of the
portal heading straight for him is just too great.  Our hero runs back
through the portal.

He must return, but first he must find some equipment and improve his
spells.

The next level (dlvl16) finally contained an alter.  But it would have
to be converted from Thoth's control.  Luckily our hero killed
something and performed the ritual.  Ah nice the alter glowed black.

The food sistuation still wasn't good, but our hero hunted for every
possible hostile on the level.  One left a ?oCM.  Standing on the
alter so he could move and coax the monster onto it, our hero read the
scroll.

Poof!  The whole room filled with monsters.  ARGH!  Now what?  He's
standing on an alter.  Can't engrave the E-word.  Can't use that wand
of digging he found.  Doesn't have a ? of teleport. #@$@# @#$@$#
@#$@#$ He just converted an alter, will he be able to #pray? Every
time I've tried it, the answer seems to be no.  But we might need to
try it this time.

Well the weakest monster is a newt to the upper right. The plan was to
kill that move onto the square and engrave like crazy.  Zap with the
force bolt.  #$@@$@# missed!  Ouch Ouch Ouch Ouch Ouch those monsters
really hurt.  Force bolt again.  This time the newt dies.  Our hero
moves quickly, but still gets hit much harder than before.  "Wizard
your life force is running out" Noooooooooo!  Finally the pounding
stops and our hero engraves the E-word!  The monsters all flee.

At this point, our hero remembers that he started out with a ?oTaming.
Talk about a "I could of had a V8" moment.

A warhorse approaches. Ah a use for the apples. Our hero and his horse
track down all the monsters and see that they are properly #offered to
the great chaotic one.

A wonderful reward is granted.  Magicbane!  "Muhahahaha, nothing can
stop me now! proclaimes our hero, "The amulet will be mine."

The last few monsters are taken to the alter and once again Anhur was
happy. But our hero is sill not strong enough to help Nefert.

He takes his horse and goes down to the next level. It was an older
and more primitive world.  Our hero got all excited when he saw what
looked like the Amulet of Yendor, then he realized it was just a cheap
plastic fake.

On to the next level. Ah a sink and a pretty little dishwasher.  Oh
yeah what an education.  Unforuntatly it wasn't educational enough.

Our hero checks out the next level.  Eeeewwwww! A disgusting nest.
Boots of stealth help here again.  "ad aerarium" is written in the
dust in this nest (WTF does ad aerarium mean?? I know it indicates a
vault teleporter.  Is it Latin or something?)

Wait what's this, our hero is slowing down.  He picked up a lizard
corpse pretty early on.  Where is it???  No no no, it's not in the
main inventory.  $#@@#$# Does he have time to check the bag?  @#$@#$@
@#$@#$ @#$@#$ Ok it's in the bag, now to get it out and eat. Oh he's
moving so slow now. Hurry Hurry Hurry!  Finally the wonderful nessage
"You feel limber!"

Now to finish off the cockatrice or flee?  This was the first time
(out of all thousand of my games) I've ever encountered the slow
stoning problem (usually it's an instakill). Our hero takes one more
whack at the yellow c and it dies!

No more of that until we have some more lizards.  Good thing the boots
of stealth kept them all sleeping.  Back out quietly and back upstairs
to the alter.  Our hero had left a few up there.

Back at the alter, he picked up the lizard corpses.  A couple new
hostiles had appeared.  Our hero used this opportunity to #pray and
make some holy water.  IIRC he also got the gift of Speed around here
too.  Our hero used another ?oCM and a /oCM for another sacfest. The
great chaotic one gave him a spellbook of identify!  With this our
hero was able to identify the amulets he had found earlier --
reflexion and life saving!  I have him use reflection since that seems
to prevent getting killed while life saving only fixes you once you
get killed.

Our hero descindes again.  He skips the rest of the nest in favor of
exploring the rest of the level.  Especially looking for the vault and
hoping that it leads to the Fort.

Bingo!  "You've penatrated a high security area" Unfortunatly, our
hero realizes he's not ready to take on this place yet.  He quickly
flees back to the main dungeon.

The next level is a swamp.  Our hero really needs something other than
force bolt to attack with.  I've lost too many chars to drowning by
eels and the like so I don't even let them get in the same room now.
Fortunatly by this time our hero was sensitive and could see where
they all were. After a tedious never ending attack of force bolts, our
hero finally kills them all.

Our hero started out with a ?oTaming.  He missed the perfect chance to
use it earlier, so he's just dying to use it now.  His horse tangles
with an Olg-hai and goes down for the count.  In my best game ever, I
had two pet Olog-hai.  Just come a little closer and let me read my
scroll.  Ah what a nice Olog-hai, fetch that ring over there. What you
don't like it, it's cursed?

Our hero picks it up and id's it as a cursed ring of levitation.  All
that holy water from earlier took care of the curse and soon he's
hapily floating in the air whenever he wants.

With a new compaion and a new ring, our hero returns to the Fort. He
greatly over estimated the Fort's defenses.  With MB, "oR, force bolt,
and the Olog-hai, the Fort fell quickly.  There was some trickyness in
the throneroom from some trolls that wouldn't die pluse the Olog-hai
couldn't cross the moat.  However Croesus proved to be a complete wimp
and died before our hero got within melee range.

Unfortunatly as our hero was counting the gold he looted, he forgot
that eventhough he ate a blue dragon near the entrance of the Fort, it
really has been a long long time since he last ate. He fainted.
Ooops.  That's when some last band of soliders appeared.  #@$@#$@#
Wake up idiot! @##@@#$ Nooooo you've got to get up!  @##@$@#$ Down to
25hp and still dropping.  Ouch 10 and droping. Whew that last one only
did 5 damage.  Finally he regains consciousness.

What to do?  They're @'s so the E-word won't help.  Eating now won't
help.  That /oDeath he picked up from a Lieutenant, will only take out
one of them, so it won't help either.  Oh wait this is a perfect
sistuation to call for devine intervention!  "Now that great Anhur has
healed me and filled my stomach, I'm going to feast on solider corpses
until I choke" proclaims our hero.  "Oh wait choking is bad, I'll just
slay y'all and let the Olog-hai feast."

Our hero now has about 60k in his bag. It's starting to get heavy even
for a blessed BoH.  Time to go back to that temple in minetown and get
rid of some of this money.  Unfortunatly, no matter what our hero did,
the Olog-hai seemed to avoid the whole area around the portal.
Eventually our hero decided to just leave the Olog-hai with the fort.

Before he left, he kicked the throne for the gems and gold.  Then he
sat on it.  He was granted a wish.  The silly idiot wished for a
blessed greased rustproof +2 Helm of Brilliance. He tought Anhur's
gift of speed was the same as having Boots of Speed.  Oh what an
idiot.  Why didn't he wish for the Boots of Speed?? The spoliers
indicate that devine Speed isn't as good as the boots.  *sigh* Oh well
he got the helm and was happy to now have an intellience of 18.

So up back to the minetown.  Our hero stopped brifely at the alter for
another mini-sacfest.  The booming voice of Anhur says "Thou art
chosen to steal souls for my glory!"  Our hero cackles out "With my
mighty finger of death spell, I shall destroy all who oppose me!" I
personally was less than happy since it was going to prolong the
process of getting create monster, magic missle, and polymorph.

While our hero was learning his new spell, he failed to notice a
baluchitherium quickly sneaking up on him.  It was horrible before he
knew it, his blood was everywhere.  Luckily the first hit with MB
scared the rhino away.  He quickly steped off the alter, engraved the
E-Word and started his studies again.  The first victim of our hero's
new spell was that rhino.  It even died on the alter, in perfect
position to thank Anhur for his great gift.

A few more #offers and our hero headed back up to the mines.  He found
the priest and started #chatting with him.  My my these priests are
all alike they just want your money.  Well it won't hurt to give him a
large chunk of gold, it might even make this BoH easier to carry.

"You contribution has been rewarded." Oh wow, our hero's AC went down
by 4!  Let's try that again and again and again...Got it down to 1 w/o
any armor and ran out of money.  Oh but wait, those evil greedy
shopkeepers, they all have lots of money and it would be great
practice for the FoD spell! Muhahahahah.  One word of note: Using FoD
one should always have reflexion as that spell seems to bounce a lot.
Our hero also rushed up to some of the upper levels and took out those
shopkeepers too.  When all was said and done hour hero probably spent
70-75k and got his base AC down to -1.

Back to the alter for another mini-sacfest and a useful spellbook,
fireball!  Our hero continued down.  He finished the cockatrice nest
being very careful and went to the next level.

Here was a gigantic throneroom with some dragons. Thanks again to the
boots of stealh (maybe it was good he did't wish for Boots of Speed)
our hero took them out one by one. After killing the 2nd dragon our
hero found himself in possession of some gray dragon scales to replace
his long lost Cloak.  He also had two blessed scrolls of enchant armor
which ended up giving him a blessed +4 gray dragon scale mail!
Woohoo! Things are still looking up.

Our hero decided to leave the rest of the throneroom and proceed down.
His new goal was to aquire teleport control then teleportis. With that
he would return to Nefret and strike down whatever evil was attacking
his former teacher.

Not far below the swamp level was Medusa's island.  Our hero entered
the level and was surrounded by a titan and many many monsters (Can
titans summon nasties??? it looks like yes they can). After engraving
the E-word, our hero tamed the warhorse that was charging him.  With
his new ally, the titan and his legions of monsters were easily taken
out.

The ring of levitation proved very useful for getting over the water.
Unfortunatly, our hero accidentally displaced the warhorse into a pool
of water.  He felt so guilty about doing that.

Our hero took out everything in the water and smaller islands and then
made his approach to Medusa's base.  He wrapped the towel around his
head and proceeded in.  There were a number of things he had to kill
to get to the central section.  However the mighty Magicbane took them
down with dispatch.

Finally he entered Medusa's lair.  As soon as he opened the door he
knew he had killed Medusa!  The amulet of reflexion once again saved
his life.  After making sure he broke apart the stone Medusa, he
removed his towel.  There wasn't too much of use in the statues.  The
cursed boots of levitation might be the only thing of note.

Our hero continued down.  The next level almost as soon as he was down
there, something locked onto his laytent telephty.  This remined our
hero that he had started out with a scroll of genocide. He used one of
his holy waters and blessed the scroll. Now the question was, should
he genocide the mindflayers or the liches?  There was definatly a
mindflayer on this level, but the liches usually prove more difficult
to kill.

Decisions, decisions.  Our hero finally decided on the L's The h's
would be for the next scroll he found.  Besides all he had to do was
just engrave the E-word and zap the FoD whenever he saw an h.

The first thing he encounted on this level was a mastodon.  The thing
hurt him bad.  Quickly he engraved the E-word and zapped off a
FoD. Then he feasted on this vile beast.

A few more nasties were dispatched to hell, Gehennom, or wherever such
things end up. Then he caught a glimps of the mindflayer.  Oh the
horror, how the heck did it get so close???  It's tentiacles tried to
grab his brain.  Fortunatly the helm of brilliance was greased.  In
spite of numerous attempts the mindflayer could never get a firm hold.
Our hero engraved the E-word and tried to zap off a FoD.  Something
didn't go right and he failed to cast the spell (how does that happen
when the spell is at 0% failure???).

The mindflayer ran off.  Our hero was careful not to follow too
closely.  He didn't want to risk the mindflayer getting a 2nd chance
now that the grease hand worn off the helm.  Finally in a long
corridor, our hero found the evil mindflayer.  The FoD spell went off
just fine this time.  Unfortunatly the mindflayer meat tasted very
bland.

With the level cleared our hero moved on down the dungeon.  After a
few more catacombs and one more bland mindflayer, our hero came to the
castle.

WTF?!? What happened to his AC?!?!? It's gone up by like 10 or 12
points!!! He's barely below zero?!?  How long has this been the
case?!?!  #@$#@@#$@#$@# @#$@@@# Was that AC boots from the priest just
temporary??  #@$$@# #@$#$@ @#$@#$@# @#$@#$#@$

Our hero took out a few monsters around the castle and in the moat.
Then he decided to return to the alter and figure out if Anhur was
angry or something.

#offering at the alter proved that Anhur was displeased.  WTF?!?
Fortunatly our hero had picked up some /oCM and soon Anhur was pleased
again.  Anhur even gave him a useful spellbook and afer another round
Anhur told him the pass tune to the castle.

Our hero then went down again.  He decided to kick the throne in the
thronroom that still had sleeping monsters. $@#@#$@#$ They all woke
up.  Fortunatly a few E-word engravings and lots of hits with
Magicbane killed them all.  Our hero got Boots of Speed from the
throne.  Unfortunatly he was again a total idiot and forgot to ask for
them to be blessed, rustproof, and +2.

Back down to the castle.  Our hero finished off the rest of the things
in the moat, with his fireball.  He tried playing the tune on his
flute, but it seemed that he was too far away from the drawbridge to
come down.  After hearing horrors of how some were crused under the
bridge, he decided to float over to the back and go in that way.

The back proved fun.  He first put the four dragons to sleep and
whacked on them until they died. He felt very firm after eating a
black dragon.  The storerooms of the castle had little of value in
them.

He pressed on to the castle's throneroom.  This turned out to be
easier than the Fort.  Fireball was very useful here as was FoD.  Soon
he had sacked the castle.  The throne disappered in a puff of logic.
He found a Wand of Wishing with three charges in it.  Some random
wands and scrolls, but nothing of extreme interest.

He was not going down to the next level.  He wanted to help Nefert
first and he also wanted to retrive that gold the priest had taken for
the temporary protection.  He thought on the next level, he could get
protection from the priest there.

So up he goes looking for tengus, leprachuans, and nymphs.  Complete
luck gave him a tengu which made him feel more in control!! Awesome.
Now it was safe to just looko for leps and nymps.  He found two
leprachauns on the next level up.  #@!@$# neither left a corpse.  The
next level up he found some sort of nymph.  @#$#@$ it didn't give him
any teleportis. The next level up he again found a leprachaun.  Ah a
corpse this time.  Wooohooo he felt very jumpy!

Now it was time to go and help Nefert. He made his way easily to
Nefert's throne.  She told him what happened with the Dark One.  Our
hero immediately went off to defeat the DO and retrieve the
Eye. Getting to the DO, fortunatly turned out to be the most uneventul
quest I've ever done (of course I can count on one hand the number of
times I've gotten this far).

Finally our hero gets to the Dark One's lair.  I was very tempted to
have our hero just teleport in, whack the DO, and teleport out, but I
figured there must be a reason for having prisoners and stuff there.
So our hero freeed all the prisoners (shouldn't he be rewarded for
this??) and killed everything hostile before coming to the alter of
the DO.  Once the DO awoke, our hero teleported to the stairs.

Then soon the DO did the same.  The battle ensued.  It was too much
for our hero and he fled upstairs to heal up.  About half the times
I've had characters fight the DO, they have killed the wimp in just a
few hits with MB.  The other half have been horrible struggles
sometimes resulting in the death of my char.  It looks like this was
going to be the latter fight.

Fortunatly while the DO followed our hero up the stairs, the DO
teleported away to the next set of upstairs. So our hero fled down and
healed up.  Once he recovered, he went back up, teleported near the
upstairs.  The DO made a fatal mistake, he moved from the stairs and
our hero took the high ground.  The fight continued.  Again our hero
